{% doc %}
  Prince Tires — Smart tire search (pt-smart-search)

  The single-input vehicle/size search, lifted out of sections/hero-smart-search
  so any hero can render it. Previously the markup, 37KB of CSS and 128KB of JS
  all lived inside that one 184KB section, which meant the search only existed
  where that section did.

  Nothing was rewritten — the markup, styles and script are byte-identical to
  what hero-smart-search shipped, just addressable:
    assets/pt-smart-search.css   the section stylesheet (flat BEM, so the rules
                                 apply wherever the markup renders)
    assets/pt-smart-search.js    the search engine — contains no Liquid, reads
                                 everything it needs from the JSON config below

  The .hero-smart-search__* class names are kept on purpose so the extracted CSS
  keeps matching. The --hero-* custom properties the styles read are set on the
  wrapper here, since the original section set them on its own root element.

  @param accent {String} optional - accent colour, defaults to brand red
  @param text {String} optional - text colour, defaults to white

  @example
  {% render 'pt-smart-search' %}
{% enddoc %}

<div
  class="pt-smart-search"
  style="--hero-accent: {{ accent | default: '#dc2626' }}; --hero-text: {{ text | default: '#ffffff' }}; --hero-bg: transparent;"
>
      <div class="hero-smart-search__search-wrapper">
        <div class="hero-smart-search__tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Search category">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="hero-smart-search__tab hero-smart-search__tab--active"
            role="tab"
            aria-selected="true"
            data-search-mode="tires"
          >Tires</button>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="hero-smart-search__tab"
            role="tab"
            aria-selected="false"
            data-search-mode="wheels"
          >Wheels</button>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-smart-search__search" data-smart-search>
          <div class="hero-smart-search__input-wrapper">
            <input
              type="text"
              class="hero-smart-search__input"
              data-smart-search-input
              placeholder=""
              autocomplete="off"
              aria-label="{{ 'sections.hero_smart_search.search_label' | t }}"
              aria-expanded="false"
              aria-controls="smart-search-results"
              role="combobox"
            >
            <span class="hero-smart-search__typewriter" data-typewriter aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {%- comment -%}
              Inline ghost-text autocomplete. Only renders when there's exactly
              one obvious completion (e.g. "2020 Honda Civi" → "c"). The prefix
              span holds the customer's typed text in transparent color so it
              measures the exact visual width — the suffix then renders muted
              right where the cursor sits. Accept with Tab or → at end-of-input.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="hero-smart-search__ghost is-hidden" data-ghost aria-hidden="true"><span class="hero-smart-search__ghost-prefix" data-ghost-prefix></span><span class="hero-smart-search__ghost-suffix" data-ghost-suffix></span></span>
            <button
              class="hero-smart-search__submit"
              data-smart-search-submit
              aria-label="{{ 'sections.hero_smart_search.search_submit' | t }}"
            >
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M4 10H16M16 10L11 5M16 10L11 15" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <div class="hero-smart-search__results" id="smart-search-results" data-smart-search-results hidden>
            <div class="hero-smart-search__loading" data-smart-search-loading hidden>
              <span class="hero-smart-search__spinner"></span>
              <span>{{ 'sections.hero_smart_search.ai_thinking' | t }}</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="hero-smart-search__results-list" role="listbox" data-smart-search-list></ul>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Discoverability hint + clickable example chips. Solves the
            most common UX gap: customers don't realize the search bar
            accepts a vehicle ("2022 Toyota RAV4") in addition to a tire
            size ("225/65R17"). Clicking a chip auto-fills the input and
            dispatches an `input` event so the existing search handler
            picks up the value and runs the query.

            Mobile: horizontal-scrolls the chip row, hides the helper
            text caret arrow, shrinks padding.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="hero-smart-search__hint" data-smart-search-hint>
            <p class="hero-smart-search__hint-text">
              Don't know your tire size?
              <span class="hero-smart-search__hint-text-mobile">Try your vehicle:</span>
              <span class="hero-smart-search__hint-text-desktop">Just type your vehicle — try one of these ↓</span>
            </p>
            <div class="hero-smart-search__chips" role="list">
              <button type="button" class="hero-smart-search__chip" data-smart-search-chip="2022 Toyota RAV4" role="listitem">2022 Toyota RAV4</button>
              <button type="button" class="hero-smart-search__chip" data-smart-search-chip="2024 Ford F-150" role="listitem">2024 Ford F-150</button>
              <button type="button" class="hero-smart-search__chip" data-smart-search-chip="2020 Honda Civic" role="listitem">2020 Honda Civic</button>
              <button type="button" class="hero-smart-search__chip" data-smart-search-chip="225/65R17" role="listitem">225/65R17</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
</div>

{%- assign hero_brands = '' -%}
{%- for f in collections.tires.filters -%}
  {%- if f.param_name == 'filter.p.vendor' -%}
    {%- for v in f.values -%}
      {%- assign hero_brands = hero_brands | append: v.label | append: '||' -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
<script data-smart-search-config type="application/json">
  {
    "minYear": {{ settings.smart_search_min_year | default: 2001 }},
    "maxYear": {{ settings.smart_search_max_year | default: 2026 }},
    "assetUrlBase": {{ 'pt-vehicle-2025.json' | asset_url | split: 'pt-vehicle-2025.json' | first | json }},
    "fallbackPhone": {{ settings.smart_search_fallback_phone | default: '403 452 4283' | json }},
    "missingVehicleWebhookUrl": {{ settings.missing_vehicle_webhook_url | json }},
    "brands": {{ hero_brands | split: '||' | json }}
  }
</script>


{{ 'pt-smart-search.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'pt-smart-search.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
